            <ArticleTitle>Demagnetizing fields in all-optical switching.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>035801</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1088/1361-648X/aa9e39</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A model of demagnetizing fields and micromagnetic simulations are applied to examine the evolution of a demagnetized cylinder. In addition to three expected final magnetic structures, a fourth switched state is obtained over a range of magnetic energy densities. The switched state is absent when demagnetizing fields are neglected. The connection to all-optical switching of materials with perpendicular magnetic anisotropy is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
